{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423025","formula":"Be₂SiO₄","hill":"Be2O4Si","elements":["Be","O","Si"],"composition":{"O":4.0,"Be":2.0,"Si":1.0},"names":{"en":"Phenakite","ru":"Фенакит","uk":"Фенакіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Phenakite or phenacite is a fairly rare nesosilicate mineral consisting of beryllium orthosilicate, Be2SiO4. Occasionally used as a gemstone, phenakite occurs as isolated crystals, which are rhombohedral with parallel-faced hemihedrism, and are either lenticular or prismatic in habit: the lenticular habit is determined by the development of faces of several obtuse rhombohedra and the absence of prism faces. There is no cleavage, and the fracture is conchoidal.","ru":"Фенаки́т (от др.-греч. φéνaξ, род. п.","uk":"Фенакі́т — мінерал класу силікатів. Ортосилікат берилію. Фенакіт — порівняно рідкісний мінерал, що містить цінний метал берилій, який легко з нього дістають, тому фенакіт являє інтерес для промисловості; використовують як дорогоцінний камінь."},"fame":32,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-3347","atoms":138,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[12.47,0.0,0.0],[-6.235,10.799,0.0],[0.0,0.0,8.247]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":5.136,"y":5.89,"z":3.445,"el":"Be"},{"x":8.767,"y":3.406,"z":3.445,"el":"Be"},{"x":4.801,"y":1.503,"z":3.445,"el":"Be"},{"x":1.099,"y":4.91,"z":4.803,"el":"Be"},{"x":-2.532,"y":7.393,"z":4.803,"el":"Be"},{"x":1.434,"y":9.296,"z":4.803,"el":"Be"},{"x":1.406,"y":2.097,"z":4.821,"el":"Be"},{"x":9.951,"y":0.169,"z":4.821,"el":"Be"},{"x":7.348,"y":8.534,"z":4.821,"el":"Be"},{"x":4.829,"y":8.702,"z":3.426,"el":"Be"},{"x":-3.716,"y":10.631,"z":3.426,"el":"Be"},{"x":-1.113,"y":2.266,"z":3.426,"el":"Be"},{"x":-1.12,"y":2.286,"z":6.186,"el":"Si"},{"x":-3.696,